      "content": "okay, thanks for getting back on track. i'll call the vet for the bloodwork and imaging. \n\nit's just that even with tests, i'm worried about things that are smart enough to hide. you talk about \"weaknesses\" of these invaders, but it feels like some of these pathogens are experts at evading the body's own defenses. they don't just sit there; they actively trick the system so they don't get caught by the immune response or show up on a scan. is there anything in biology that actually behaves like that—something that's basically a master of evasion and can stay totally undercover while it's actively causing damage?",
